{
  "esm": "0.8.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "ReSEACT3D",
    "description": "ReSEACT 3-D transport on a 7x7x7 NATIVE slice of the GEOS-FP 4x5 grid centred over the central US, driven by real GEOS-FP meteorology. NO REGRIDDING: the local grid IS the native grid (lon cells 15..21 -> centres -110..-80; lat points 30..36 -> 26..50; levels 1..7, k=1 = surface), so the whole conservative-overlap chain collapses to an index shift.\n\nTransport is the monotone flux-form PPM stack imported BY REFERENCE from EarthSciDiscretizations: regional open-wall inflow BCs on lon/lat, and the HYBRID sigma-pressure massform vertical (dp = dA[k] + dB[k]*PS(i,j,t)) on lev. The horizontal and vertical rule stack is byte-identical to the verified prototypes/transport_3d/transport_3d.esm; only the FORCING differs — the analytic test winds and constant PS are replaced by GEOS-FP U/V/OMEGA/PS, each supplied by an EarthSciIO discrete_provider returning the TWO records bracketing the solver time and blended continuously in time (records_per_sample=2 + w_time, the era5 pattern).\n\nGEOS-FP's collections are not co-phased, so three independent weights are used: w_I3 (PS, 3-hourly instantaneous at 00:00Z), w_A3 (U/V/OMEGA, 3-hourly means at 01:30Z) and w_A1 (PBLH, hourly means at 00:30Z).\n\nFace fluxes follow the metric the ESD divergence stencils imply on the unit sphere: Mx = dp_face*U_face/a and My = dp_face*V_face/a (Pa/s, matching m in Pa), with the A-grid GEOS-FP winds averaged to faces. Mz = -OMEGA (OMEGA is dP/dt, +ve DOWNWARD; Mz is +ve UPWARD at each cell's LOWER edge).\n\nCAVEATS. (1) PS is read in hPa and scaled by 100 — the loader declares Pa but EarthSciIO returns raw file values. (2) The lev no-flux BC is baked into the stencils (they never read Mz[1] or Mz[NLEV+1]), so the 7-level slab is CLOSED at its ~906 hPa top even though real air flows through it — a truncated-column artifact, negligible over the 1 s first-light window but not for long runs. (3) The two end lat rows are half-width (lat_edge clamps them) while native lat cells are a full 4 deg. (4) Using OMEGA directly means m drifts from dp: the mass fluxes are not the ones that reproduce the observed surface-pressure tendency (Jockel et al. 2001). CWC still holds EXACTLY — both continuity and tracer use the same fluxes — which is what the q == 1 gate tests.",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": [
      "esd:problem",
      "grid:latlon3d",
      "family:finite_volume",
      "op:D",
      "axes:lon,lat,lev",
      "scheme:flux_form",
      "property:free_stream",
      "bc:inflow"
    ]
  },
  "models": {
    "GEOSFP": {
      "ref": "../../../EarthSciModels/components/earthsci_data/geosfp.esm"
    },
    "Transport3D": {
      "expression_template_imports": [
        {
          "ref": "../../../EarthSciDiscretizations/grids/latlon3d/rules/face_flux_divergence_lon_open_bc.esm",
          "bindings": {
            "NLON": 7,
            "NLAT": 7,
            "NLEV": 7
          }
        },
        {
          "ref": "../../../EarthSciDiscretizations/grids/latlon3d/rules/face_flux_divergence_lat_open_bc.esm",
          "bindings": {
            "NLON": 7,
            "NLAT": 7,
            "NLEV": 7
          }
        },
        {
          "ref": "../../../EarthSciDiscretizations/grids/latlon3d/rules/ppm_flux_D_lon_mono_inflow_bc.esm",
          "bindings": {
            "NLON": 7,
            "NLAT": 7,
            "NLEV": 7
          }
        },
        {
          "ref": "../../../EarthSciDiscretizations/grids/latlon3d/rules/ppm_flux_D_lat_mono_inflow_bc.esm",
          "bindings": {
            "NLON": 7,
            "NLAT": 7,
            "NLEV": 7
          }
        },
        {
          "ref": "../../../EarthSciDiscretizations/grids/latlon3d/rules/ppm_flux_D_lev_mono_hybrid_noflux_bc.esm",
          "bindings": {
            "NLON": 7,
            "NLAT": 7,
            "NLEV": 7
          }
        },
        {
          "ref": "../../../EarthSciDiscretizations/grids/latlon3d/rules/face_flux_divergence_lev_massform_noflux_bc.esm",
          "bindings": {
            "NLON": 7,
            "NLAT": 7,
            "NLEV": 7
          }
        }
      ],
      "variables": {
        "m": {
          "type": "state",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "lon",
            "lat",
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Air mass per cell (a pressure thickness). Strictly positive."
        },
        "mq": {
          "type": "state",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "lon",
            "lat",
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Tracer mass per cell. Initialised bitwise equal to m, so q == 1."
        },
        "dev": {
          "type": "state",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "lon",
            "lat",
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Diagnostic deviation dev = mq - m, obtained by integrating the DIFFERENCE of the two right-hand sides from dev(0) = 0. This is the quantity the conformance assertion gates: at q == 1 the tracer divergence collapses bitwise onto the continuity divergence, so dev's own right-hand side is EXACTLY 0.0 in IEEE and dev never leaves zero. It exists because assertion `reference` expressions are build-time and cellwise and cannot read states or observeds, so q itself is not assertable and asserting mq would require re-spelling the entire discrete divergence by hand -- i.e. duplicating the operator inside its own test. Against a constant-zero reference there is nothing for the test to get wrong. dev feeds nothing back into m or mq."
        },
        "lon0_deg": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "deg",
          "default": -112.5,
          "description": "West EDGE of the slice. GEOS-FP 4x5 lon cell edges are -182.5+5*(i-1); -112.5 is the edge of native cell i=15, so cells i=15..21 (centers -110..-80) map to lon_local 1..7 with NO interpolation."
        },
        "lat0_deg": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "deg",
          "default": 26.0,
          "description": "Southern-most lat POINT of the slice. GEOS-FP 4x5 lat points are -90+4*(j-1); 26 is native j=30, so points j=30..36 (26..50) map to lat_local 1..7 with NO interpolation."
        },
        "dlon_deg": {
          "type": "observed",
          "units": "deg",
          "expression": 5.0,
          "description": "GEOS-FP 4x5 native zonal spacing. Open west/east walls (regional, not periodic)."
        },
        "dlat_deg": {
          "type": "observed",
          "units": "deg",
          "expression": 4.0,
          "description": "GEOS-FP 4x5 native meridional spacing. Open south/north walls (regional, not polar)."
        },
        "phie": {
          "type": "observed",
          "units": "deg",
          "shape": [
            "lat_nodes"
          ],
          "description": "Latitude cell EDGES from the grid's lat_edge template; the half-polar caps fall out of the clamp at +/-90.",
          "expression": {
            "op": "apply_expression_template",
            "args": [],
            "name": "lat_edge",
            "bindings": {}
          }
        },
        "coslat_e": {
          "type": "observed",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "lat_nodes"
          ],
          "description": "cos of the latitude edges. Zero-length face at each pole. Never read at faces 1 or NLAT+1 -- the pole terms are structurally omitted.",
          "expression": {
            "op": "apply_expression_template",
            "args": [],
            "name": "coslat_edge",
            "bindings": {
              "phie": "phie"
            }
          }
        },
        "dS_lat": {
          "type": "observed",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "lat"
          ],
          "description": "Exact spherical cell-area weight sin(phie[j+1]) - sin(phie[j]).",
          "expression": {
            "op": "apply_expression_template",
            "args": [],
            "name": "latcell_area",
            "bindings": {
              "phie": "phie"
            }
          }
        },
        "dphi_lat": {
          "type": "observed",
          "units": "rad",
          "shape": [
            "lat"
          ],
          "description": "Meridional cell extent; HALF-width at the two polar caps.",
          "expression": {
            "op": "apply_expression_template",
            "args": [],
            "name": "latcell_dphi",
            "bindings": {
              "phie": "phie"
            }
          }
        },
        "Mx": {
          "type": "observed",
          "units": "Pa/s",
          "shape": [
            "lon_nodes",
            "lat",
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Zonal face-normal AIR-MASS flux (Pa/s) at each lon face: Mx = dp_face * U_face / a, the metric the ESD divergence stencil implies on the unit sphere (cell area dlon_rad*dS_lat, zonal face length dphi_lat). dp_face and U_face are 2-point averages of the two native cells flanking the face (13+ie, 14+ie) — exact, because each local lon cell has the same footprint as native cell 14+i and the local edges sit on native cell midpoints. Replaces the Stage-B analytic wind. The west/east wall faces (ie=1, ie=NLON+1) are GENUINE faces on an open domain, and their halo cells (native 14 and 22) exist in the native array — no extrapolation needed.",
          "expression": {
            "op": "aggregate",
            "output_idx": [
              "gie",
              "gj",
              "gk"
            ],
            "args": [
              "F_PS",
              "F_U",
              "dA",
              "dB"
            ],
            "ranges": {
              "gie": {
                "from": "lon_nodes"
              },
              "gj": {
                "from": "lat"
              },
              "gk": {
                "from": "lev"
              }
            },
